# CQ-04 · frame-style
#
# Question: Which scenes declare a rendering style, and which style does the
#           composition say it renders as?
# Persona:  P3 — director / creative technologist. Style is a separate frame
#           from the depicted world (§3.1), which is what lets a shot be
#           re-rendered in another medium without touching the scene.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §5.3.2 (`vso:VisualStyle`); §5.2 (`vso:rendersAs`)
# Form:     SELECT — one row per declared VisualStyle
# Note:     `vso:framedBy` attaches a style; `vso:rendersAs` picks the one the
#           composition is rendered in. A document may declare several and
#           render as one, so the two columns are asked separately.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

SELECT ?doc ?style ?aesthetic ?palette ?medium ?rendersAs
WHERE {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?scene a vso:Composition ; vso:framedBy ?style .
    ?style a vso:VisualStyle .
    OPTIONAL { ?style vso:aesthetic ?aesthetic }
    OPTIONAL { ?style vso:palette   ?palette }
    OPTIONAL { ?style vso:medium    ?medium }
    OPTIONAL { ?scene vso:rendersAs ?rendersAs }
  }
}
ORDER BY ?doc ?style
